      "message": "Nit: `syntax_raw` is public, and it can now run an epoch: at the cap, under a counting strategy, outside a run. Until now a `_raw` call never freed anything, and `generate-temporaries` still says so (\"nothing is collected, so the values stay valid\"). That one is safe, since natives run with `running` set. But a host calling `syntax_raw` from Rust while it holds other values raw, not in handles, can have them freed. That\u0027s worth a line in the doc comment.",
